{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling for every lane, after H's static unit ended with exit 1\n(a3e2c83a): run the cheap checks as working checks first.\n\n1. Before a sealed unit of any kind, run these on the head as ordinary\n   working checks: `git diff --check`, the commit-message check,\n   `npm run format:check`, the link checker and the notes check. Each\n   takes seconds. They need no packet, freezer, seal or audit.\n2. Do the same with each compiler config that reads a changed file, as\n   ruling 1ce32e09 says for G.\n3. A sealed unit starts when those pass. Its packet is the evidence.\n4. Count from this night: G had three sealed failures at one compiler\n   config, one at a stale link and one at a generated reference file,\n   and H has one at a subject line of 101 characters. A working check\n   finds each of them in under a minute.\n\nYour repair of the two merge subjects is right: reword only those two\ncommits, keep every tree, and keep the original head under a backup\nref until H lands.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}